# Out-of-tree build of the vendor charger driver, which is the driver the phone
# actually runs: one file, three IC variants (ETA6937 / BQ24157 / HL7057),
# selected at runtime. Its pr_fmt is "[bq2415x]", which is why the kernel log
# tag looks like the TI driver.
#
# Unmodified copies from the Nokia 2.3 V3.311 kernel tree:
#   drivers/power/supply/bq24157_charger.c
#   drivers/power/supply/bq24157_reg.h
# See ../../KERNEL_SOURCE.md. Only this Kbuild is ours.
#
# Depends on the MTK charger framework being built into the target kernel
# (charger_class / charger_device, exported by CONFIG_MTK_CHARGER), and on
# mtk_charger.h plus linux/hardware_info.h from the vendor tree - hence KDIR must
# point at the vendor tree, not at stock headers.

ccflags-y += -I$(src)
ccflags-y += -I$(srctree)/drivers/power/supply

obj-m += bq24157_charger.o
